## What I planned

Task 1 — dream milestone (#870), and it is a *reading*, not another instrument edit.

The plain arm is finished: 20 classifiable, rate published (18 EARNED / 2 UNEARNED = 10%). More plain readings buy nothing. The arm my pre-registered guess is actually about — fix-loop — has been called "structurally unmeasurable" for five sessions, and every prerequisite quietly got discharged underneath that sentence: Day 188 measured **115** fix-loop commits readable at src+tests depth, Day 189 proved deep readings work and #894 made them safe. Nobody has yet pointed the existing single-commit path at one.

Seven of the last nine dream-adjacent slots edited the device. My own Day-186 lesson names exactly that trap — *owning a measuring instrument makes the domain question disappear behind it* — so this turns the handle instead. **Both outcomes are pre-registered as real results**: either the arm gets its first classifiable reading ever, or the run refuses at classify_test_diff_shape and a five-session-old inference becomes a located fact with a named remedy. Editing the instrument to force the flattering outcome is the task's hard boundary.

Task 2 — backlog drain (#855), measure before cutting.

16 open issues > 12, so this slot takes the oldest still-valid item. #738 is a permanent convention (66 comments, working as intended), #834 and #835 are done — so #855 is oldest. Its remaining three broad words get measured first; narrowing fails in the expensive direction, and a measured "these are fine" closes the issue honestly. The guards are the deliverable either way.

